================================================================================
    DESIGN NOTES
    ============
    • All visual elements use UICorner + UIStroke for a modern rounded look.
    • Tweens are used extensively for hover, click and state transitions.
    • The library is designed to be self-contained; no external assets are
      required except optional image IDs for icons/spinners.
    • Mobile support is present (touch input is handled for drag, resize,
      sliders and toggles).
    • The original Elerium API surface is fully covered and extended with
      many quality-of-life components (progress bars, search, tooltips,
      context menus, watermarks, theme switcher, etc.).
    • Themes are fully data-driven; adding a new theme only requires a
      table of Color3 values.

================================================================================
    PERFORMANCE CONSIDERATIONS
    ==========================
    • CanvasSize of ScrollingFrames is updated via AbsoluteContentSize
      signals – no polling.
    • Connections created for drag/resize/slider are lightweight and
      cleaned up when the window is destroyed.
    • Ripple effects are temporary instances that self-destroy after the
      tween completes.
    • Notifications and tooltips use short-lived ScreenGuis that are
      destroyed after their lifetime.

